# Bot2 casts Deep-Cavern Bat on turn four. With its enters trigger on the stack (Bot1 passes once, so the Bat
# resolves first), Bot1 flashes in Tishana's Tidebinder off a Black Lotus and counters that triggered ability. The
# Bat is a creature, so it loses all abilities for as long as the Tidebinder remains: no flying or lifelink, and the
# Lightning Bolt in Bot1's hand is never looked at or exiled. That still holds a turn later.
#
# On turn five Bot1 bolts its own Tidebinder. Once it has left the battlefield the Bat has its abilities back.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
